---
code: cli-stdin-claimed-twice
when-fires: two lanes of one invocation both want stdin. cli/lib.rs parse_args_from, over the claimants `stdin_claimants` collects. {first} and {second} name them, in argv-then-lane order.
why: 30I §2.5 — stdin is a collapsed SINGLE resource, so every mode wanting it declares its claim and two claimants refuse before network naming both, rather than resolving by a precedence rule the reader would have to know.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- cli-stdin-claimed-twice && mise run loom:promote -- cli-stdin-claimed-twice`; prove it stuck with `mise run test`, which is also what catches anything else the promotion moved. `mise run loom:vars -- --all cli-stdin-claimed-twice` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
